The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```dts
&gpio0 {
	ti,no-idle-on-init;
	ti,no-reset-on-init;
```
Reason:
The flags `ti,no-idle-on-init` and `ti,no-reset-on-init` were incorrectly placed at the GPIO0 node level instead of the interconnect target module level. This misplacement caused warnings because these flags are intended to control the behavior of the interconnect target module, not the GPIO node itself.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```dts
+&gpio0_target {
	ti,no-reset-on-init;
```
Reason:
The patch moves the `ti,no-reset-on-init` flag to the correct interconnect target module level (`&gpio0_target`), which resolves the warnings by ensuring that the flags are applied to the appropriate module, thereby controlling the intended behavior correctly.

